WEBVTT

00:08.759 --> 00:10.761
[intriguing music playing]

00:30.113 --> 00:31.114
[smacks lips]

00:37.454 --> 00:38.455
[sighs]

00:39.581 --> 00:41.750
[phone ringing]

00:47.631 --> 00:48.632
Hello?

00:51.468 --> 00:54.721
I… I can… I can barely hear you.

00:56.682 --> 00:57.683
What?

01:00.102 --> 01:01.103
Where?

01:02.187 --> 01:04.815
I've been asleep for a day?

01:12.865 --> 01:14.741
[intriguing music continues]

01:44.021 --> 01:49.401
The entry mentioned a plague,
which Gerrie connected to 1702.

01:50.402 --> 01:51.612
And with that,

01:52.237 --> 01:56.450
we are able to deduce that the journal
belonged to Sarah Westcott Warren.

01:56.533 --> 01:58.118
And, um…

01:58.660 --> 01:59.870
- Here.
- [Patricia] Oh.

02:01.330 --> 02:02.915
[breathing shakily]

02:02.998 --> 02:05.334
[liquid splashing]

02:06.543 --> 02:08.336
[Patricia sipping]

02:14.718 --> 02:15.719
Thank you.

02:16.720 --> 02:21.642
We thought maybe the cursed item might
be buried with Richard Warren.

02:22.809 --> 02:25.687
So Wyck suggested we dig him up.

02:26.563 --> 02:28.148
And so, we did just that.

02:30.567 --> 02:32.194
You-You did what?

02:33.362 --> 02:34.988
We dug up Richard Warren's coffin.

02:38.408 --> 02:40.410
You dug up the founder's corpse?

02:40.494 --> 02:42.246
- Yeah, it's over there.
- Yeah, it's here.

02:42.913 --> 02:43.914
[stammers]

02:55.259 --> 02:56.593
Are you out of your fucking minds?

02:56.677 --> 02:58.512
[Wyck] All right, just listen
to what she's telling you.

02:58.595 --> 03:00.681
- Oh, my God. He's in there?
- [Wyck] No. He's upstairs.

03:00.764 --> 03:02.349
- [Patricia] We moved him.
- [Wyck] Mm-hmm.

03:03.559 --> 03:05.435
[stammers] Why, um…

03:05.519 --> 03:07.813
Whoa. Why-Why did you move him?

03:07.896 --> 03:09.189
Because he's still alive.

03:11.149 --> 03:12.484
What?

03:12.568 --> 03:16.780
But we have been able
to communicate a little through notes.

03:19.950 --> 03:20.951
- What?
- [sighs]

03:21.034 --> 03:24.538
Richard Warren is in that room.

03:24.621 --> 03:25.664
He's waiting for you.

03:25.747 --> 03:28.458
- [Wyck] Hmm.
- [stammers] What do you me…

03:28.542 --> 03:30.085
Why would he be waiting for me?

03:30.169 --> 03:33.463
He will only communicate with the "Lord
Island Protector." We assume that's you.

03:33.547 --> 03:35.924
Yeah, look at this. See this?

03:36.008 --> 03:37.009
Huh?

03:37.634 --> 03:38.927
[grunts]

03:39.011 --> 03:40.554
Yeah. Yeah.

03:41.722 --> 03:42.723
[sighs]

03:42.806 --> 03:43.974
You go in there

03:44.892 --> 03:46.935
and get him to tell you

03:47.561 --> 03:49.521
how the fuck to open this thing.

03:51.732 --> 03:53.275
- No!
- No, no, no! No!

03:53.942 --> 03:55.277
Don't…

03:55.360 --> 03:57.029
Don't try to do it yourself.

03:57.779 --> 03:58.989
Get him to do it.

03:59.698 --> 04:00.699
Here.

04:10.918 --> 04:12.920
[door creaking]

04:17.507 --> 04:19.051
[breathes deeply]

04:51.500 --> 04:53.210
I'll give you two your privacy.

04:54.336 --> 04:55.337
[door locks]

05:21.530 --> 05:22.906
[breathes deeply]

05:46.889 --> 05:48.056
[exhales deeply]

06:35.521 --> 06:37.064
[breathes shakily]

06:47.407 --> 06:48.700
Oh, I forgot one thing.

06:55.707 --> 06:57.251
[breathes deeply]

06:58.335 --> 07:00.087
You-You-You can talk?

07:02.214 --> 07:03.215
[Richard] Aye.

07:03.715 --> 07:05.050
[sighs]

07:07.803 --> 07:09.221
How, um…

07:11.974 --> 07:13.684
How are you still alive?

07:16.228 --> 07:22.359
I was tricked by a devil
and betrayed by my lessers.

07:23.193 --> 07:26.363
But an evil power sustains me.

07:28.073 --> 07:30.534
What-What do you mean?
Is that… Is that what this is?

07:32.703 --> 07:33.745
Is it?

07:36.582 --> 07:39.501
Ca-Can… Can you open this?

07:47.968 --> 07:49.595
Loosen these.

07:53.098 --> 07:54.641
Sure, yeah. Um… I mean… [stammers]

07:54.725 --> 07:57.436
Well, I can… I can l-loosen them a-a bit.

08:12.492 --> 08:14.453
Yeah, l-let's…
Yeah, let's get those off you.

08:17.164 --> 08:18.165
[sighs]

08:29.051 --> 08:30.052
[Richard grunts]

08:35.390 --> 08:37.558
[disembodied gasping]

08:44.816 --> 08:45.901
What is this?

08:47.778 --> 08:51.031
I thought it was my salvation.

08:52.950 --> 08:56.537
We couldn't even find vermin
to sate our hunger.

08:57.788 --> 08:59.957
Some ate the corpses,

09:00.541 --> 09:03.001
others gorged on dirt.

09:03.794 --> 09:10.259
I was contemplating how to end my own life
with my own hand when I saw it.

09:15.764 --> 09:17.099
[whispering] Sorry, forgot my purse.

09:19.560 --> 09:20.561
[door locks]

09:25.858 --> 09:27.150
What, um…

09:28.819 --> 09:30.320
What was it you saw?

09:30.863 --> 09:32.865
[Richard breathes deeply]

09:33.407 --> 09:36.159
A simple morsel of food.

09:37.369 --> 09:39.079
A mushroom.

09:40.664 --> 09:42.165
I thanked God.

09:43.542 --> 09:46.545
But something else came to me.

09:52.759 --> 09:54.178
Wh-What was it?

09:57.598 --> 09:58.599
A demon?

10:00.058 --> 10:01.852
The island itself?

10:03.478 --> 10:08.609
But I was starving,
and it was starving too.

10:09.943 --> 10:14.656
The covenant was offered
for my settlement's salvation,

10:14.740 --> 10:18.076
and I signed that pact

10:18.160 --> 10:23.373
with my own blood, feces and semen.

10:35.844 --> 10:38.055
What did you offer in return?

10:39.056 --> 10:41.391
If I had refused,

10:42.476 --> 10:44.478
- none of you would be here.
- [scoffs]

10:45.729 --> 10:47.314
Maybe that would've been better.

10:47.981 --> 10:53.487
Oh, it's easy to judge when
your island is flourishing around you.

10:53.570 --> 10:54.655
Flourishing?

10:56.114 --> 11:00.244
My son is stuck on a fucking hell rock.

11:01.328 --> 11:04.248
[breathes heavily]

11:08.126 --> 11:10.546
I think it spoke to me.

11:11.839 --> 11:12.840
Oh?

11:15.425 --> 11:16.426
Did you follow it?

11:16.510 --> 11:17.511
No.

11:20.305 --> 11:21.974
What did it want?

11:23.475 --> 11:29.481
It knows frightened men
will do desperate things.

11:31.775 --> 11:33.068
What does that mean?

11:36.154 --> 11:39.157
I want to see my children's things.

11:41.451 --> 11:44.454
- [Richard breathing heavily]
- [footsteps staggering]

12:00.095 --> 12:02.097
[breathing shakily]

12:07.477 --> 12:09.813
Every second in that coffin,

12:10.814 --> 12:12.774
I imagined their deaths.

12:16.987 --> 12:18.989
[breathing shakily, sniffling]

12:23.785 --> 12:24.786
[grunts]

12:38.217 --> 12:39.218
[sniffs]

12:50.896 --> 12:51.897
[whimpers]

12:56.235 --> 12:57.861
[whispering] Sarah.

13:04.368 --> 13:06.370
[sobbing]

13:08.747 --> 13:10.249
Oh, so sad.

13:12.793 --> 13:14.795
[straining]

13:19.132 --> 13:20.133
[Patricia] Oh.

13:20.217 --> 13:23.220
[Richard breathes heavily, panting]

13:31.228 --> 13:33.146
As long as there are men with my blood,

13:33.897 --> 13:37.276
you are bound to the covenant.
But I am the last.

13:38.402 --> 13:39.778
What are you saying?

13:41.029 --> 13:42.447
Take me out to sea,

13:43.365 --> 13:47.661
past the point where sailors fear.

13:49.246 --> 13:50.998
Once I am beyond its grip,

13:52.499 --> 13:54.168
without the hex upon me,

13:55.335 --> 13:58.630
I believe I will age and die.

13:59.798 --> 14:01.717
With my bloodline gone,

14:02.217 --> 14:05.971
my death will free the island
from its curse.

14:08.223 --> 14:10.767
First of all,
we don't know that this will kill him.

14:10.851 --> 14:12.519
There's only one way to find out.

14:12.603 --> 14:15.898
Second of all,
the island's not gonna let him go easy.

14:15.981 --> 14:17.858
It's dangerous enough out there.

14:17.941 --> 14:21.528
At sea, at night,
let alone sailing with weak men.

14:21.612 --> 14:23.697
And no, I'm not talking about him.

14:23.780 --> 14:25.824
Anything can happen out there.

14:25.908 --> 14:29.745
The fact that you don't know that
tells me how dangerous this really is.

14:32.372 --> 14:33.373
[scoffs]

14:34.625 --> 14:35.626
Last night…

14:37.085 --> 14:38.295
[exhales]

14:39.379 --> 14:40.631
I felt a presence.

14:40.714 --> 14:41.715
I did.

14:42.382 --> 14:44.801
I don't know what it is
and I don't know what it wants.

14:45.594 --> 14:47.179
I know we have to end it.

14:48.430 --> 14:50.015
I know we have to try.

14:57.272 --> 14:59.775
He's not on my boat
unless he's in the goddamn coffin.

15:03.612 --> 15:04.613
[Tom] Um…

15:05.489 --> 15:08.325
W-W-Wyck will take us out.

15:08.867 --> 15:12.579
B-But there will be people on the dock.

15:12.663 --> 15:18.961
So I have to ask, would you be w-willing
to get back inside the coffin?

15:19.545 --> 15:22.422
Just… Just until we're on the boat.

15:26.385 --> 15:28.345
- Just until we're on the boat.
- Yeah.

15:33.141 --> 15:35.102
- [grunts]
- Yeah. Okay.

15:36.395 --> 15:37.396
[Patricia] Tom.

15:42.150 --> 15:44.152
[vehicle approaching]

15:45.028 --> 15:46.029
[Tom gasps]

15:46.113 --> 15:47.781
[whispering] Oh, shit.

15:47.865 --> 15:49.116
What's he doing here?

15:50.075 --> 15:53.620
Someone may have reported my screaming.
Let me talk to him.

15:53.704 --> 15:55.247
What? H-H-Hold on. Hold on.

15:55.330 --> 15:56.331
- Tom.
- [grunts]

15:57.332 --> 15:58.333
I got this.

16:01.295 --> 16:03.839
[door opens, closes]

16:06.258 --> 16:09.511
[Patricia] Well, Patricia strikes again.

16:09.595 --> 16:12.472
Lost my keys, found my keys.
It was great to see, uh…

16:12.556 --> 16:13.724
Have a good night.

16:13.807 --> 16:14.975
[Bechir] All right. You too.

16:15.058 --> 16:16.143
- [Patricia] Yeah.
- You…

16:27.237 --> 16:28.739
You should just go home.

16:28.822 --> 16:29.823
[Bechir stutters]

16:31.366 --> 16:32.367
[stutters]

16:33.744 --> 16:34.745
Patricia.

16:35.245 --> 16:37.206
Come here. Get out of my Jeep.

16:37.289 --> 16:39.374
- [engine starts]
- [Bechir] What the hell are you doing?

16:39.458 --> 16:40.751
Patricia.

16:40.834 --> 16:41.960
Come here. Get…

16:44.129 --> 16:46.131
- I swear to God…
- Oh, my God.

16:47.674 --> 16:49.593
[Bechir] Patricia,
what the hell are you doing?

16:49.676 --> 16:51.470
You better listen. Patricia!

16:52.554 --> 16:54.389
Stop this! Sto… Stop this!

16:54.890 --> 16:55.974
Come here!

16:56.558 --> 16:57.559
Let's go.

16:58.727 --> 17:00.729
[tense music playing]

17:02.606 --> 17:04.608
[groaning]

17:36.682 --> 17:41.520
Lot of fishermen learn the hard way
that you don't go too far from the island.

17:41.603 --> 17:45.524
It's like our own Bermuda Triangle
out there.

17:46.608 --> 17:47.776
[sighs]

17:48.402 --> 17:52.739
So, we'll stop two minutes
before we get to this line.

17:54.575 --> 17:56.952
That's the dead zone.

17:57.035 --> 17:58.954
Crossing it will trigger this light.

18:00.747 --> 18:05.669
Beyond this buoy, people like me
don't tend to come back.

18:08.088 --> 18:11.842
Anyway, I'm gonna stop the boat
at the two-minute mark.

18:11.925 --> 18:16.263
You can put him on the dinghy from there
and take him the rest of the way yourself.

18:17.347 --> 18:20.392
Is-Is two minutes cutting it too close
for you?

18:21.977 --> 18:24.646
You won't be able to row
on that thing much longer.

18:27.816 --> 18:32.154
Let's get him past the buoy and
send him to hell so we can end all this.

18:34.239 --> 18:36.617
The devil has hovered over this city,

18:37.117 --> 18:38.368
made it his own.

18:38.952 --> 18:40.996
The people in it are his.

18:41.496 --> 18:44.833
Evil has triumphed over good here.

18:45.709 --> 18:47.461
Look at my church.

18:47.544 --> 18:49.171
I have no parish…

18:49.963 --> 18:52.716
I have… I have weed. If you… If you want.

18:52.799 --> 18:55.552
We-We just have to smoke it outside.

18:56.970 --> 18:59.056
Your dad isn't coming home soon, is he?

18:59.139 --> 19:00.766
No, no, no. Not for a while.

19:02.392 --> 19:03.685
[actor] Good evening. Good evening.

19:03.769 --> 19:04.978
What's his deal? [chuckles]

19:06.355 --> 19:07.731
I don't know. I…

19:10.359 --> 19:12.903
I used to think that
he was scared of everything.

19:12.986 --> 19:15.072
But now I just think he's a liar.

19:19.910 --> 19:20.994
Wanna find out?

19:25.374 --> 19:27.167
[smacks lips] Is his room upstairs?

19:28.794 --> 19:32.172
[stutters] Kelly, um… Okay. Um…

19:32.256 --> 19:35.968
Leave Whitewood tonight. I beg of you.

19:36.051 --> 19:40.180
- What power?
- Leave before it is too late.

19:41.640 --> 19:44.601
Kelly, I don't… I don't…
I don't think that we should go in there.

19:46.478 --> 19:48.981
If he's really lying to you,
he can't punish you.

19:49.565 --> 19:51.775
It's called the moral high ground.

19:55.612 --> 19:58.115
[Patricia crying, sniffling]

20:14.923 --> 20:16.466
[stammers]

20:17.301 --> 20:19.469
[sobbing] You're not taking me in?

20:20.387 --> 20:21.763
No.

20:21.847 --> 20:24.183
'Cause I can't listen to this all night.

20:26.143 --> 20:28.687
But I'm at my wits end, Patricia.

20:29.313 --> 20:31.398
Getting all kind of weird calls now.

20:31.899 --> 20:33.650
Fucking pulling people out the ocean.

20:33.734 --> 20:35.819
I need to know what the hell is going on.

20:36.320 --> 20:37.571
I don't know what you mean.

20:37.654 --> 20:41.366
Oh. Oh, I think you know
exactly what I mean.

20:41.867 --> 20:45.162
And I know you loyal to Loftis,
but people are talking,

20:46.288 --> 20:49.291
forming some kind of
action committee or some shit,

20:49.374 --> 20:50.792
and hey, I can't blame 'em.

20:51.293 --> 20:54.171
Nobody's been able to reach the guy
for the last 24 hours.

20:54.254 --> 20:56.089
They just don't understand
what he's doing.

20:56.173 --> 20:58.258
Well, make me understand what he's doing.

20:59.176 --> 21:00.177
Huh?

21:01.345 --> 21:05.390
Because if I don't,
it's dangerous for myself, my wife,

21:05.474 --> 21:07.267
and every person on this island.

21:08.310 --> 21:10.687
I can't.
They told me not to cause a panic.

21:10.771 --> 21:15.067
[Bechir] Oh, Jesus Christ.
What might I panic about?

21:20.989 --> 21:22.032
Come on, Patricia.

21:24.493 --> 21:26.620
You know I've always been on your side.

21:37.214 --> 21:38.340
[huffs]

21:42.553 --> 21:43.804
- [radar beeping]
- [static on radio]

21:43.887 --> 21:45.514
[person 1 speaking indistinctly on radio]

21:45.597 --> 21:48.141
…approximately one mile
to the island. Low visibility.

21:48.225 --> 21:51.520
[person 2 speaking indistinctly on radio]

21:51.603 --> 21:53.730
[indistinct chatter on radio]

21:55.399 --> 21:56.441
What? What is that?

21:56.525 --> 21:58.235
The island playing games.

21:58.318 --> 22:01.488
- [engine revs, sputters]
- [Wyck grunting]

22:03.615 --> 22:04.825
Make sure…

22:04.908 --> 22:07.578
Make sure that coffin is secure.

22:07.661 --> 22:09.121
I'm gonna check below.

22:12.541 --> 22:13.542
[pants]

22:28.265 --> 22:29.933
- [Richard] Who goes there?
- [exhales]

22:31.602 --> 22:32.811
[knocks on coffin]

22:32.895 --> 22:33.896
[Richard] Hello.

22:34.855 --> 22:36.064
I know it's you.

22:36.940 --> 22:37.941
Please.

22:38.775 --> 22:39.902
Say something.

22:40.944 --> 22:43.697
- I feel like I'm suffocating!
- [stammers] Everything's fine. Just…

22:43.780 --> 22:46.783
- Just take deep breaths.
- [Richard panting]

22:46.867 --> 22:51.079
[Richard] Thank God. Oh, thank God.
God bless you.

22:54.458 --> 22:56.126
Are you going to let me out now?

23:01.215 --> 23:04.176
Look, I can't. And I-I-I am… I'm so sorry.

23:08.096 --> 23:10.140
- It's what you promised.
- Yes, I-I know.

23:10.224 --> 23:14.478
I… I realize that, but I…
and I am… I am so sorry.

23:18.315 --> 23:19.483
[Richard] Oh, fuck you.

23:21.610 --> 23:23.904
- Fu-Fuck me?
- Yes. I said, "Fuck you."

23:24.655 --> 23:25.739
Fuck you!

23:25.822 --> 23:28.033
[Richard scoffs] Fuck me? Fuck you!

23:28.116 --> 23:29.535
Fuck off.

23:33.539 --> 23:34.915
[Richard] Are you still here?

23:36.667 --> 23:39.169
Uh… He-He's… He's asking to be let out.

23:41.338 --> 23:44.132
I will never understand
how the fuck you got your job.

23:44.216 --> 23:46.009
[chuckles]

23:46.093 --> 23:47.719
Why are you even bringing this to me?

23:48.929 --> 23:50.514
- He hasn't asked for much. He--
- Yeah.

23:50.597 --> 23:55.519
It starts as one thing and then another.
I am not letting that thing loose.

23:56.186 --> 23:58.939
Nah, you can't trust a man
that knows death's coming for him.

23:59.022 --> 24:01.275
Well, it-it's hard--

24:01.358 --> 24:03.902
Yeah, well of course it is!
Course it fucking is!

24:09.324 --> 24:10.659
[sighs]

24:22.087 --> 24:23.088
Here.

24:26.967 --> 24:29.970
My best friend, Mark Doyle,
and his sister.

24:31.513 --> 24:32.723
My girl, Gerrie.

24:36.768 --> 24:37.936
Gerrie Doyle?

24:39.021 --> 24:40.230
[smacks lips] That's right.

24:42.816 --> 24:44.318
M-Museum Gerrie?

24:44.902 --> 24:45.903
That's the one.

24:46.778 --> 24:48.947
Gerrie Doyle from the Historical Society?

24:49.031 --> 24:50.574
- I said that's the one.
- Sorry.

24:56.288 --> 24:57.664
I was just 16.

24:59.166 --> 25:01.210
It was a bad time on the island.

25:01.293 --> 25:02.294
[chuckles]

25:04.296 --> 25:05.797
So the island's on lockdown.

25:07.090 --> 25:10.469
There's curfews, uh… people going missing.

25:12.095 --> 25:15.516
The perfect time for a fishing expedition.

25:15.599 --> 25:16.975
[laughs]

25:17.059 --> 25:19.645
Me and my four buddies,
we decide to steal a boat,

25:19.728 --> 25:22.439
get it out on the white waves,
test our mettle.

25:22.523 --> 25:23.732
Yeah. Yeah.

25:26.276 --> 25:29.488
It struck from below at first.
Struck hard.

25:30.155 --> 25:31.823
This thing was big.

25:32.407 --> 25:34.618
It was gonna tear the boat apart
in seconds.

25:35.327 --> 25:36.995
And then I hear Ricky say he saw…

25:38.455 --> 25:40.749
saw a tentacle. [chuckles]

25:41.500 --> 25:45.754
Just like that, we become little boys
again screaming for our mothers,

25:45.838 --> 25:46.839
and I… [sniffles]

25:46.922 --> 25:51.593
…and I'm… I know
I-I-I-I gotta get outta there. [chuckles]

25:51.677 --> 25:55.430
You know, before the whole thing sinks.
Before we're dragged into its mouth.

25:56.139 --> 25:58.475
And, so, I start to swim off.

25:59.935 --> 26:03.480
And that…
that's when I felt it grab my foot.

26:04.606 --> 26:05.983
[breathes shakily]

26:06.066 --> 26:07.484
I was so scared.

26:07.568 --> 26:10.737
I mean, it's… it's pulling on me,
and I'm trying to get away.

26:12.614 --> 26:17.786
And then I realize it's Mark,
begging for help.

26:19.204 --> 26:20.205
And now,

26:21.707 --> 26:23.750
we're both getting pulled under and I…

26:24.418 --> 26:26.670
and I see that thing below him.

26:27.629 --> 26:30.591
We're both getting dragged down,
and I… and I…

26:36.013 --> 26:37.264
I kicked him off me.

26:39.600 --> 26:40.684
Kicked him off me.

26:43.979 --> 26:47.024
- Wyck, that wasn't your fault.
- [chuckles]

26:47.107 --> 26:50.903
I only told you that story so that
you'll listen to me one fucking time.

26:50.986 --> 26:53.405
Do not let him out!

26:56.200 --> 26:58.785
I-I-I already let him out.

27:08.462 --> 27:10.214
He can barely stand.

27:11.590 --> 27:13.133
Goddamn you to hell.

27:13.759 --> 27:15.594
Yeah. Yeah.

27:28.857 --> 27:29.858
[Kelly gasps]

27:29.942 --> 27:32.778
Oh. [laughs] Yeah.

27:35.239 --> 27:36.782
- [box clacking]
- Oh.

27:37.491 --> 27:39.493
They only lock it if there's a secret.

27:55.425 --> 27:57.427
[chuckling]

28:07.521 --> 28:09.147
Is that your mom?

28:10.732 --> 28:12.234
She was so pretty.

28:21.118 --> 28:23.412
I thought you said
she died during childbirth.

28:27.332 --> 28:28.333
She did.

28:41.638 --> 28:42.764
I knew her.

28:44.725 --> 28:46.393
Well, this is sadder
than I thought it'd be.

28:46.476 --> 28:48.312
I thought it'd be like a fun secret.

28:49.479 --> 28:53.066
[Patricia] Yes, so my theory is
that the island corrupts.

28:53.150 --> 28:54.902
And maybe that's
what would've happened to me.

28:54.985 --> 28:58.780
I would have just been
another horrible incident in our history.

28:59.489 --> 29:00.741
Who can say?

29:00.824 --> 29:01.825
[sighs]

29:01.909 --> 29:04.411
Okay, yeah, I know what that sounds like,
I… I get it.

29:04.494 --> 29:07.915
Patricia's crazy. That's… That's fine.

29:16.381 --> 29:18.800
Yeah. [sighs heavily] I'm out.

29:20.344 --> 29:21.470
Do you believe me?

29:21.553 --> 29:23.055
I just don't care to find out.

29:24.181 --> 29:27.059
[clicks tongue] Didn't like it here before
and don't like it much more now.

29:27.142 --> 29:29.186
Well, I really have only told you
the half of it--

29:29.269 --> 29:30.562
And guess what?

29:30.646 --> 29:31.730
I'm good.

29:32.397 --> 29:35.817
[laughs] See. I'm-I'm-I'm good.

29:35.901 --> 29:37.986
I don't need nothing.
I don't need the other half.

29:38.070 --> 29:39.071
Do me a favor.

29:39.655 --> 29:43.116
Why don't you give my friend, the mayor,
my week's notice.

29:43.200 --> 29:44.201
That's it.

29:44.701 --> 29:45.702
- Huh?
- Okay.

29:45.786 --> 29:48.789
And, uh… feel free to help yourself out.

29:49.706 --> 29:51.917
- Okay.
- The damn thing's broken anyway.

29:52.000 --> 29:53.335
[door opens]

29:53.836 --> 29:55.462
It might be fine tomorrow.

29:55.546 --> 29:57.881
[stammers] Yeah, well, uh…

29:58.465 --> 29:59.716
That sounds promising.

30:00.217 --> 30:02.636
Mmm. And good luck to you all.

30:05.514 --> 30:06.723
- Thank you.
- Mm-hmm.

30:14.273 --> 30:16.275
[moaning]

30:28.036 --> 30:30.038
[moaning continues]

30:36.378 --> 30:37.713
- [sighs]
- [clears throat]

30:37.796 --> 30:39.715
♪ Oh, come, lads ♪

30:39.798 --> 30:44.344
♪ Let's earn our wage today ♪

30:44.928 --> 30:48.140
♪ Who will be the last man? ♪

30:48.223 --> 30:49.808
You know that one, Wyck?

30:49.892 --> 30:50.976
Uh-huh.

30:51.059 --> 30:57.441
♪ We'll board our ship and sail today ♪

30:57.983 --> 31:02.362
♪ Who will be the last man? ♪

31:08.744 --> 31:11.371
[breathes deeply]

31:15.042 --> 31:17.044
[moaning]

31:23.550 --> 31:24.843
[Wyck] We're getting close.

31:26.220 --> 31:27.888
Get the dinghy ready.

31:30.557 --> 31:32.809
I wonder what my last words will be.

31:35.312 --> 31:36.939
Will I think of my children?

31:38.524 --> 31:43.403
Hmm. Something trivial?
Some petty grievance?

31:46.490 --> 31:47.908
Will I think of my mother?

31:52.454 --> 31:54.456
Or will I say, "Please, God,

31:56.166 --> 31:57.251
let me live"?

32:05.259 --> 32:08.345
You know, if-if I made it to 60,
I'd be more than happy.

32:08.428 --> 32:09.930
[boat creaks]

32:10.013 --> 32:12.015
[grunting]

32:16.103 --> 32:17.396
[grunts]

32:18.856 --> 32:20.607
[engine sputters]

32:20.691 --> 32:22.943
[grunting]

32:23.026 --> 32:25.028
[eerie music playing]

32:32.703 --> 32:33.704
[scoffs]

32:36.206 --> 32:37.583
[sipping]

32:43.922 --> 32:46.175
[Wyck gasps] No, no, no, no, no…

32:46.258 --> 32:48.260
[grunting, panting]

32:59.188 --> 33:01.773
[ominous music playing]

33:13.118 --> 33:15.037
[breathes deeply, sighs]

33:18.081 --> 33:19.291
Let's keep going.

33:25.964 --> 33:27.799
[engine starts]

33:31.970 --> 33:34.890
[Wyck] ♪ The skipper calls ♪

33:36.225 --> 33:40.020
♪ For a starboard tack ♪

33:41.522 --> 33:46.610
♪ But who will be the last one? ♪

33:48.487 --> 33:52.199
♪ The eastern wind ♪

33:52.282 --> 33:54.701
♪ Can't hold us back ♪

33:55.827 --> 33:58.539
♪ Though the fish are few ♪

33:59.456 --> 34:02.334
♪ And the water black ♪

34:03.126 --> 34:05.254
- [humming]
- We're gonna need a different plan.

34:07.464 --> 34:09.174
- [Richard grunts]
- [Tom groans]

34:10.467 --> 34:12.844
[Wyck] You son of a bitch! Give me that!

34:12.928 --> 34:14.888
- [Richard] I wanna live!
- [Wyck] Give me that!

34:14.972 --> 34:18.809
[Richard] Let go of me, you giant bear!
Let me go, you fucker!

34:18.891 --> 34:21.061
- I'm gonna make you eat my dick!
- [Wyck grunting]

34:21.143 --> 34:23.146
[both grunting]

34:24.815 --> 34:26.233
[Wyck] Goddamn it!

34:28.235 --> 34:30.987
- Get the harpoon! Now!
- [Richard growls]

34:31.071 --> 34:33.866
- [grunting, shouting continues]
- [grunting]

34:36.368 --> 34:39.746
[Richard] I don't wanna die!
I don't wanna die!

34:46.085 --> 34:48.422
[engine sputters]

34:52.676 --> 34:54.011
[engine stops]

34:54.594 --> 34:55.596
[pants]

35:00.100 --> 35:01.101
[groans]

35:13.530 --> 35:15.532
[panting]

35:16.491 --> 35:18.493
[grunting]

35:19.286 --> 35:20.787
[harpoon fires]

35:24.666 --> 35:27.294
- [groaning]
- [Richard breathing heavily]

35:33.050 --> 35:35.344
[shouting]

35:36.887 --> 35:38.972
[Tom straining]

35:39.473 --> 35:41.225
[Wyck shouts]

35:41.767 --> 35:43.769
[all grunting]

35:45.437 --> 35:49.274
- [Tom] Get him in the coffin!
- [Richard] No! No, no, no!

35:49.358 --> 35:51.193
- Stay there.
- There!

35:51.276 --> 35:53.403
[groaning, shouts]

35:56.657 --> 35:59.493
- [Richard] Let me live! [groans]
- [Wyck grunts]

35:59.576 --> 36:00.577
Let me live!

36:01.828 --> 36:04.456
Let me live!

36:04.540 --> 36:06.083
- [groaning]
- [Wyck] Lay down!

36:10.546 --> 36:12.965
- [Richard shouting]
- [wind howls]

36:13.048 --> 36:14.842
[Wyck shouting]

36:15.425 --> 36:18.345
- [shouts]
- [grunting]

36:18.428 --> 36:20.430
- [Tom straining]
- [banging on coffin]

36:21.557 --> 36:23.934
- [Richard] I don't wanna die!
- [alarm blaring]

36:29.648 --> 36:30.983
- [grunts]
- [gasps]

36:31.066 --> 36:32.150
- Oh, thank y--
- [grunts]

36:32.234 --> 36:33.277
[yells]

36:36.488 --> 36:38.532
- [banging continues]
- [muffled shouting]

36:38.615 --> 36:39.908
[straining]

36:40.742 --> 36:43.579
[Richard, distorted] Let me live!

36:43.662 --> 36:44.663
[banging stops]

36:46.957 --> 36:48.333
[rattling]

36:56.383 --> 36:58.385
[dramatic music playing]

37:05.350 --> 37:07.269
- [music fades]
- Shit. Shit.

37:07.352 --> 37:09.354
[alarm continues]

37:10.105 --> 37:11.148
[sighs] Shit.

37:11.231 --> 37:13.233
- [panting]
- [engine starts]

37:14.526 --> 37:16.528
[tense music playing]

37:24.661 --> 37:25.954
Damn it.

37:27.706 --> 37:29.708
[panting]

37:35.005 --> 37:36.173
[alarm stops]

37:44.640 --> 37:45.724
Wyck!

37:45.807 --> 37:47.142
[panting]

37:48.435 --> 37:49.645
Wyck!

37:52.022 --> 37:53.524
Wyck!

37:56.527 --> 37:58.779
- [whale calls]
- [panting]

38:08.997 --> 38:10.999
[grunts, panting]

38:23.470 --> 38:24.471
[thuds]

38:26.640 --> 38:28.642
[gasping, grunting]

38:29.893 --> 38:31.144
- [laughs]
- [hopeful music playing]

38:31.228 --> 38:32.980
- I thought you were dead!
- [Wyck] Yeah?

38:33.063 --> 38:35.899
- Then what are you doing down there?
- I-I was… I was looking for flares.

38:35.983 --> 38:38.694
Yeah, so they can find you? Damn it all.

38:39.403 --> 38:42.781
This shit… [groaning]

38:43.282 --> 38:45.158
Why did you move that?

38:45.242 --> 38:46.660
[switches clink, engine starts]

38:47.619 --> 38:49.621
[panting]

38:52.916 --> 38:53.917
[sighs]

39:06.763 --> 39:07.890
You did good.

39:11.185 --> 39:12.186
Thank you.

39:15.063 --> 39:16.857
I did very fucking good.

39:17.524 --> 39:19.526
[both laughing]

39:24.364 --> 39:26.074
Wait, did you check the coffin?

39:26.158 --> 39:27.743
- Oh, yeah.
- [grunts]

39:27.826 --> 39:29.786
Just a lot of ribs and Vienna sausage.

39:29.870 --> 39:31.914
[laughing]

39:32.956 --> 39:34.249
At least he's done singing.

39:34.333 --> 39:35.918
[laughing continues]

39:39.463 --> 39:41.465
[dramatic music playing]

40:13.830 --> 40:17.042
Huh, yeah, perfect.
You kicked my suitcase down the stairs,

40:17.125 --> 40:20.045
- you clubfooted moron.
- It just fell. Excuse me, it fell.

40:20.128 --> 40:23.006
You have castoring rollers on the bottom,
which are a menace.

40:23.090 --> 40:24.925
This is the worst inn I've ever stayed in.

40:25.008 --> 40:28.762
- Good. Then you can leave.
- You smell like cabbage took a shit…

40:28.846 --> 40:30.430
- That's…
- …in a baby's diaper.

40:44.111 --> 40:47.990
[singing a cappella]
♪ Come lads let's earn our wage today ♪

40:48.073 --> 40:51.159
♪ Who will be the last man? ♪

40:51.243 --> 40:55.289
♪ We board the ship and sail today ♪

40:55.372 --> 40:58.292
♪ Who will be the last man? ♪

40:58.375 --> 41:01.795
♪ The eastern wind can't hold us back ♪

41:01.879 --> 41:06.300
♪ Though the fish are few
And the water is black ♪

41:06.383 --> 41:09.887
♪ The skipper calls for a starboard tack ♪

41:09.970 --> 41:13.390
♪ But who will be the last man? ♪

41:13.473 --> 41:17.436
♪ We drink our share of rum and ale ♪

41:17.519 --> 41:20.522
♪ Cup shot to the last man ♪

41:20.606 --> 41:24.568
♪ In a mighty storm of rain and hail ♪

41:24.651 --> 41:27.696
♪ Fighting to the last man ♪

41:27.779 --> 41:31.617
♪ We're drunk as sows
When the sun goes down ♪

41:31.700 --> 41:35.662
♪ Far and away from our island town ♪

41:35.746 --> 41:39.291
♪ The skipper walks the plank and drowns ♪

41:39.374 --> 41:42.836
♪ But who will be the last man? ♪

41:42.920 --> 41:46.798
♪ Ten days adrift at sea today ♪

41:46.882 --> 41:49.927
♪ Who will be the last man? ♪

41:50.010 --> 41:53.597
♪ The widows weep at home and pray ♪

41:53.680 --> 41:57.059
♪ That theirs will be the last man ♪

41:57.142 --> 42:00.687
♪ A hunger creeps for men asleep ♪

42:00.771 --> 42:05.108
♪ And when they wake I bare my teeth ♪

42:05.192 --> 42:08.445
♪ The blood and bile o'er deck they seep ♪

42:08.529 --> 42:12.241
♪ For I become the last man ♪
